// LSASS Memory Access with Read Rights
// Detects credential dumping by flagging process handle access to lsass.exe with read rights (Sysmon Event ID 10), excluding known security products. Tool-agnostic: catches Mimikatz, procdump, comsvcs, and custom loaders alike.
// techniques: T1003.001   severity: high   status: stable
// validate: Atomic Red Team T1003.001
//   procdump.exe -accepteula -ma lsass.exe C:\Windows\Temp\l.dmp
// source: rules/credential-access/lsass-handle-access.yml  (GENERATED, do not edit by hand)
SecurityEvent
| where (((TargetImage endswith "\lsass.exe") and (GrantedAccess =~ "0x1010" or GrantedAccess =~ "0x1410" or GrantedAccess =~ "0x143a" or GrantedAccess =~ "0x1438")) and not ((SourceImage endswith "\MsMpEng.exe" or SourceImage endswith "\wmiprvse.exe")))
